{"findings": [{"title": "The real forge reader accepts the first attestation for a digest without checking its predicate type", "specimen": ".attavo/bin/forge-attestation:23 and bin/attavo:1116", "retires": "The assumption that any JSON attestation stored under the synthetic merge digest proves the Attavo traversal was sealed.", "rejection_test": "test_forge_attestation_ignores_unrelated_predicate_types", "severity": "Blocking when the digest has an unrelated attestation\u2014especially when it is first in the API response\u2014because doctor reports the item sealed without an Attavo statement."}, {"title": "The merge-group doctor races the workflow that creates the attestation", "specimen": ".github/workflows/ci.yml:32 and .github/workflows/attavo-coherence.yml:114", "retires": "The assumption that enabling the new proof in merge-group CI guarantees the statement is already readable.", "rejection_test": "test_merge_group_doctor_runs_only_after_attestation_is_published", "severity": "Blocking when the doctor job reads the merge-group digest before the independent coherence workflow finishes actions/attest@v2; the valid merge group fails nondeterministically with a 404."}, {"title": "Complete items are silently omitted unless one merge introduced every stage record", "specimen": "bin/attavo:1160", "retires": "The claim that the proof accounts for every merged, fully staged item rather than only the repository's customary single-merge record layout.", "rejection_test": "test_doctor_proof_six_fails_when_stage_records_arrive_across_multiple_merges", "severity": "Blocking when an item's four stage records reach the branch across multiple merges or direct commits and another item satisfies proof two; merge_introducing_records returns null, the item is skipped, and doctor can report done without checking its seal."}], "tests_named": ["test_forge_attestation_ignores_unrelated_predicate_types", "test_merge_group_doctor_runs_only_after_attestation_is_published", "test_doctor_proof_six_fails_when_stage_records_arrive_across_multiple_merges"]}